Rejects an expression that nests more than 64 arrays or objects, counting
those in its literal values and in a legacy filter. Parsing recurses at each
level, about 1.3 KB of stack apiece, so a deeply nested expression overflowed a
thread's stack and crashed instead of failing to parse; a 128 KB musl thread
held about 95 levels
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1432).
Upstream: not proposed

